comments:
Tavern is THE Nashville brunch spot.

{starters}
I have tried a good portion of the starter selections - but the buffalo cauliflower, brussels and tavern fries stand out above the rest. The mussels are also a great option for dinner or happy hour. 

{entrees}
I'm a huge fan of benedicts, and Tavern kills it with each of their 3 options - aptly named uno, dos, and (for some reason) three. Uno is my favorite, with braised short rib and Tobasco hollandaise. It is absolutely delicious. Other great options are the Nooner - which is a bacon scramble with fried oysters and spicy sour cream - and the Singapore Stir-fry, with wok-style rice, a sunny-side-up egg, and bacon. You really can't go wrong with any of the Tavern's fantastic brunch selections, but these stand out for sure.

{libations}
Possibly the reason that Tavern is so popular among Nashville brunch-goers, is the 2-for-1 deal they offer during brunch all weekend. The selection is fairly standard, with mimosas, a bellini, two bloody mary renditions, and a very sweet sangria. My favorite is the blood orange mimosa, but each drink has its merits.

Overall, Tavern is a wonderful place for any brunch occasion and I will continue to dine here often as long as I am in Nashville. The wait is brutal so make sure you arrive early to start off with a beverage in the sun on their outdoor waiting area. Enjoy!

